.TH FPACRTD 1 "9 October 2026" Linux "FPAC Operator's Manual"
.SH NAME
fpacrtd \- dynamic ROSE routes daemon of the FPAC node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fpacrtd [-c <filename>] [-f] [-n] [-t] [-v]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
.B fpacrtd
exchanges ROSE routes with the direct neighbours of the node. Each node
announces the destinations it can reach, learns the ones it lacks and
installs them in the ROSE routing table of the kernel.
.P
Only two kinds of destinations are exchanged: the full address of a node
(10 digits) and a whole DNIC (4 digits). A route written in
.B fpac.routes
always keeps the last word: a destination found there with the same
address and the same length is never installed by
.B fpacrtd.
.P
.B fpacrtd
is started and stopped by
.B myfpac.sh
with the other FPAC daemons. It does nothing and exits at once when
neither
.B RouteAnnounce
nor
.B RouteLearn
is set, so a node that does not use dynamic routes is not affected.
.P
This daemon is new in FPAC 4.2 and still experimental.
.SH OPERATION
.LP
The neighbours are the adjacent nodes declared in
.B fpac.nodes.
A neighbour takes part only when its Node block carries
.B Route = yes.
The others are never called, and a call from a node that is not a
declared, participating neighbour is refused.
.P
The sessions are ROSE connections to the service callsign
.B FPACRT.
The first call is made 30 seconds after the start, to let the neighbours
start their own daemon. A neighbour that does not answer within 120
seconds, or that closes the session, is called again 30 minutes later.
.P
The cost of a route is a number of hops. A destination is announced with
the cost of this node, the neighbour adds one, and a route of more than
6 hops is dropped. A destination is never announced to the neighbour it
is reached through.
.P
A full table is sent when a session opens and every 30 minutes after
that. Changes in between are sent about 10 seconds after they happen. A
learned route is removed when the neighbour withdraws it, when it has
been missing from 3 full tables in a row, or as soon as the session with
that neighbour closes. A neighbour from which routes were learned and
that has sent no full table for 90 minutes has its session closed, and
is called again 30 minutes later.
.P
Every minute
.B fpacrtd
checks that the routes it installed are still in the kernel, and puts
back any that disappeared. When it stops it removes all of them. The
routes it has installed are also written to a state file, so that the
next start can remove what a crash would have left behind.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.LP
The keywords below are read by
.B fpacrtd
itself in
.B fpac.conf
and
.B fpac.nodes.
The other FPAC programs ignore them.
.TP 20
.BI "RouteAnnounce = yes|no"
send the table of this node to its neighbours. Default: no.
.TP 20
.BI "RouteLearn = no|nodes|all"
learn nothing, only node addresses, or node addresses and whole DNICs.
Default: no.
.TP 20
.BI "RouteOrigin = <dnic>"
announce this node as the exit gateway of a DNIC (4 digits). One line
per DNIC. The line is ignored, with a warning in the log, unless
.B fpac.routes
holds a route to that whole DNIC. The DNIC is announced only while a
neighbour of that route is open (restarted) in the kernel, and withdrawn
when the exit link closes; each change is written in the log.
.TP 20
.BI "Route = yes"
inside the Node block of a neighbour: exchange routes with it.
.P
.B Route = yes
must be written only for a neighbour that runs
.B fpacrtd.
A node without it does not refuse a call to the FPACRT service: it
handles it as a call from a user.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP 20
.BI "\-c <filename>"
also read the Route keywords of this file. Meant for trials, to keep
them out of fpac.conf.
.TP 20
.BI \-f
stay in the foreground and also print the log to the terminal
.TP 20
.BI \-n
dry run: exchange tables but never change the kernel routes, and do not
write the state file
.TP 20
.BI \-t
show the configuration as it was read (node, neighbours, origins) and
exit
.TP 20
.BI \-v
verbose mode: log every line sent and received, and a summary of each
full table
.SH FILES
.I /etc/ax25/fpac.conf
.br
.I /etc/ax25/fpac.nodes
.br
.I /etc/ax25/fpac.routes
.br
.I /var/ax25/fpac/fpacrt.dat
(routes installed by the daemon: address, length, neighbour, device)
.br
.I /var/ax25/fpac/fpacrtd.lock
(held locked while the daemon runs; a second
.B fpacrtd
finds it locked, reports
.I another fpacrtd is already running
and exits with status 1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.LP
Messages go to syslog with the tag
.B fpacrtd.
Without
.B \-v
they report the start and the stop, each session opened or closed, and
each route added to or removed from the kernel.
.SH SEE ALSO
fpad(1) fpacwpd(1) fpacroute(1) myfpac.sh(1) fpac.conf(5) fpac.nodes(5)
fpac.routes(5)
.P
The specification is in the file
.I dynamic-routes.md
of the FPAC documentation.
